    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50893" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vĭenna</span></b> , ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				city in</i> Gallia Narbonensis, <i>on the
			Rhodanus</i>, now <i>Vienne</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 7,
				9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 10, 9, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 5,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 47, 46, § 121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 4, 5, § 36</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Mart. 7, 88, 2 al.</span></i>—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vĭennensis</span></b> ,
				e, adj., <i>of</i>
			 or <i>belonging to Vienne</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 1, 3, § 18</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vĭennenses</span></b> ,
			ĭum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Vienne</i>, <i><span class="en">Vell. 2,
			121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 1, 65</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 14,
				4, 6, § 57 al.</span></i></div>
